/target
/models
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED, deliberately. dlm ships binaries -- prebuilt release
# assets and `cargo install` -- and the convention for an application is to lock
# its dependency graph rather than re-resolve it per build. Ignoring it meant
# every CI run and every published binary was built against whatever crates.io
# happened to serve that day, and it is how the MSRV broke unnoticed: clap's
# `"4"` drifted to a clap_lex that requires 1.85 while the manifest still said
# 1.75. Nothing observed the change because nothing recorded the old answer.
